{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 32, :comments ["<b>These are the counted ones of the children of Israel</b> etc., <b>six hundred thousand and three thousand and five hundred and fifty.</b> He has already mentioned this number above, and the reason it was repeated a second time is to indicate the mighty wonder that was among them: for not one of them died from this great nation from the day they were counted until the day of the journey's departure, and it was twenty days — for they journeyed on the twentieth of the month."], :book :numbers, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:29:43.735321252Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}